
The macOS GPUIOverlayView event-registration pattern and deferred scene-plane
architecture in this change were adapted from the Apache-2.0 GPUI crates in
https://github.com/egoist/zed at 57bd4fe181639797d395978d5de17bc9e10a6219.
The overlay input policy, Metal integration and lifecycle adaptations are Zeron
changes.

`crates/gpui/src/bounds_tree.rs` (a balanced tree, and last frame's orderings
replayed while bounds repeat), the per-size native font in
`crates/gpui_macos/src/text_system.rs`, and grouping sprites by texture in
`crates/gpui/src/scene.rs` are adapted from the Apache-2.0 GPUI fork
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-fast at 8eed010 (bounds tree), a9a9533
(fonts) and ceb4795 (sprites).

Demand-driven Windows frames are adapted from the Apache-2.0 GPUI fork
https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-fast at 124f79b ("schedule Windows frames on
demand") and ec3f4a3 ("avoid redundant Windows frame requests after input"):
the frame wake, per-window frame request and device-removal wake in
`crates/gpui_windows/src/frame_schedule.rs` and `device_wake.rs`, their hooks
in `platform.rs`, `window.rs`, `events.rs` and `direct_manipulation.rs`, the
native checks in `native_tests.rs` and the idle benchmark in
`examples/windows_idle_frames.rs`. Harness drives the requests from zui's
`frame_requester` and `pause_frame_requests` hooks instead of re-arming after
every present, and leaves out the GPU-reset test case.
